{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1103701-primal-urge","id":1103701,"title":"Primal Urge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-14T20:33:14-07:00","id":1103701,"title":"Primal Urge","content":"So one talent that has often been overlooked in my gaming experience is primal urge. People buy it up, but it tends to only come up when shifting or activating a gift. Are there any other moments people use primal urge for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T20:51:21-07:00","id":1103704,"title":"","content":"It is the default skill to use most times a character is in lupus form. If you are in lupus form, anytime you're hunting, tracking, or trying to survive, primal urge is the skill to do so as the actual abilities a human would use are based on rational thought and training. All those kind of skills for a wolf are bundled in Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> And of course, any application of animal magnetism would use it.<br /> <br /> It's also something I've occasionally called for to do a gut instinct reaction check to see if the sub conscious notices something amiss and overrides the conscious mind with a warning or insight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T00:01:02-07:00","id":1103739,"title":"","content":"I think it depends a lot on how you or your ST handles the divide between Primal Urge and Survival for 'mundane' rolls; because there's a lot to be had there. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> <br /> noted, there's plenty of examples of using Primal Urge in the W20 core book either as an option between it and Survival, or based on your current form. There's even an option for replacing Alertness with Primal Urge in certain circumstances.<br /> <br /> Another point to note though, is that Primal Urge is supposed to also be a weak version of the Awareness Talent that can pick up very simple cues that something supernatural is going on, so characters should get a Perception + Primal Urge roll to get a sense of supernatural activity. In any WtA game where the PCs are regularly dealing with subtle supernatural threats, Primal Urge is going to be a very valuable thing to have for noticing stealthier enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}